WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
The results are encouraging.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.900
Drawing one thousand twenty-four noise realizations
from SLIC,

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.152
its power spectrum matches a Welch estimate from
real LIGO data,

00:00:10.232 --> 00:00:15.734
and it resolves narrow spectral lines even more
finely thanks to more training data.

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.395
Injecting a known signal,

00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:21.581
SLIC recovers all five varied parameters with high
credibility,

00:00:21.661 --> 00:00:25.700
and its posterior is tighter than the
Gaussian-likelihood one.
